    <briefdescription>
<para>A very primitive implementation of lock-free LIFO (last in first out, AKA stack, AKA single-linked list with head-only add and remove). </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>It is only usable to store free pages of a memory allocator or similar, since it assumes that all addresses are aligned, and lower 16 bits of address can be used as a counter-based solution for ABA problem. </para>    </detaileddescription>
